Always request the thread-safe errno.

illumos <errno.h> gives a translation unit the thread-safe errno only under
_REENTRANT, _TS_ERRNO or _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 199506L, and this spec defines
_REENTRANT only for -pthread. Everything else gets libc's global `errno`
object, which is also where the main thread's errno lives, so a library built
without -pthread overwrites the main thread's errno from whichever thread it
runs on. _TS_ERRNO changes errno and nothing else.

The nixpkgs cc-wrapper passes -D_TS_ERRNO too; this covers the unwrapped
compiler and gcc's own target libraries (libquadmath imported plain errno).

--- a/gcc/config/sol2.h
+++ b/gcc/config/sol2.h
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 
 #undef CPP_SUBTARGET_SPEC
 #define CPP_SUBTARGET_SPEC "\
-%{pthreads|pthread:-D_REENTRANT -D_PTHREADS}"
+-D_TS_ERRNO %{pthreads|pthread:-D_REENTRANT -D_PTHREADS}"
 
 /* Names to predefine in the preprocessor for this target machine.  */
 #define TARGET_SUB_OS_CPP_BUILTINS()
